  "source": "Goldman Sachs",
  "title": "IG Credit - Too Much, Too Fast",
  "type": "credit",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-07-12",
  "insights": [
   "IG credit is bifurcating into two markets: AI/Tech and Traditional, with the AI basket widening ~25bps despite better ratings and massive equity market caps.",
   "The market is struggling to absorb the deluge of AI-related issuance, which has reached $360B over the past year; investors are signaling that funding another $360B in the next 12 months will be difficult.",
   "Hyperscaler and chip-maker debt now accounts for 9% of the IG index on a dv01 basis, exceeding the concentration of the Big 6 US Money Center banks.",
   "To absorb future AI buildout financing, the market requires slower supply, more forward guidance, a shift toward shorter duration/EUR-denominated issuance, and increased private credit/bank-intermediated funding.",
   "The author expects further underperformance in AI-related credit in the medium-to-long term due to the supply picture, while favoring owning credit volatility for broader IG.",
   "The author anticipates AI credit curves will continue to steepen, while generic IG 5s/30s curves may flatten as investors sell non-AI 5yr cash to fund AI-related purchases."
